    "https://careers.utoledo.edu/jobs/clinical-research-program-manager-health-science-campus-college-toledo-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "UToledo Careers",
      "description": "Clinical Research Program Manager - Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United States Back to UToledo Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode UToledo Careers Clinical Research Program Manager 501477 Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH Administration Full-Time None Research Show More Show Less Staff - Full-Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: Clinical Research Program Manager Department Org: Jacobson Clinical Research Center - 107980 Employee Classification: J1 - Salaried Full Time HSC Bargaining Unit: Professional Staff Association Primary Location: HSC C Shift: 1 Job Description: This role is responsible for leading the clinical trials operations team and providing oversight for clinical research coordinating staff for supported groups. The position provides expert advice to University of Toledo (UToledo) faculty and principal investigators (PIs), clinical research coordinators, leadership and other personnel involved in the execution of clinical trials throughout the lifecycle. This position maintains a working knowledge on current regulations and University policies that govern the administration of clinical research. This position will work collaboratively with the Clinical Research Information and Financial Manager to engage PIs across the institution in the growth of clinical research. This position must communicate effectively with university personnel and administrative departments as well as external sponsors and contract research organizations. This position provides training on policies, and procedures as needed. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in nursing, public health, healthcare management, business management or a related discipline. • Minimum of five (5) years of professional and functionally relevant experience. • Demonstrated experience in training of personnel. • Knowledge of academic medical center standard practices and policies, including but not limited to Medicare Coverage Analysis, Fair Market Value and Standard of Care. • Knowledge of FDA and Good Clinical Practice guidelines and regulations. • Experience with medical coding and knowledge of medical terminology. • Proficient in electronic health information systems (i.e., EPIC), Microsoft Office suite, and ability to learn and use other software systems as required by the position. • Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. • Background with federal and non-federal regulations for grant and contract management Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated independent decision-making abilities. Ability to work in a team environment under stressful and time-sensitive conditions. • Previous work history demonstrating strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. • Ability to manage competing priorities and meet time-sensitive deadlines. • Ability to maintain a strong customer-service oriented environment. • Must have strong verbal and written communication skills with a demonstrated ability to communicate effectively. • Must be able to work in collaboration with others at various levels both within and outside the University. • Demonstrated attention to detail with a high level of initiative. Conditions of Employment: To promote the highest levels of health and well-being, the University of Toledo campuses are tobacco-free. Pre-employment health screening requirements for the University of Toledo Health Science Campus Medical Center will include drug and other required health screenings for the position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Toledo is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Toledo does not discriminate in employment, educational programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, ancestry, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military or veteran status, disability, familial status, or political affiliation. The University is dedicated to attracting and retaining the best and brightest talent and fostering a culture of respect. The University of Toledo provides reasonable accommodation to individuals with disabilities. If you require accommodation to complete this application, or for testing or interviewing, please contact HR Compliance at hrcompliance@utoledo.edu or 419-530-4747 between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5 p.m. or apply online for an accommodation request. Computer access is available at most public libraries and at the Office of Human Resources located in the Center for Administrative Support on the UToledo Main Campus. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 077eff28 Last Name (required) 7b4162a6 Email (required) d76a5e96 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended jobs Cardiac Sonographer 2 Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Heart Station - 109070 Cardiac Sonographer 2, Full Time (8:00am - 17:30pm) 5 8's Saturday rotation\nNo Sundays, Call is on rotation, Holiday call is on rotation.\nMay Underfill with Cardiac Sonographer 1. Ekg Technician I Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio Heart Station - 109070 EKG Technician I, Part Time, Sunday - Saturday (6:30am - 11:00pm).\nRotate, Weekends/Holidays. Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio. Health Science Campus Hospital Toledo, OH, Ohio. Health Science Campus Support Toledo, OH, Ohio Dept. of Cell and Cancer Biology - 107500 Cell & Cancer Biology Faculty Position Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6bc376ab Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Full-Time None Research Administration Full-Time None Research Employment Type Staff - Full-Time Staff - Full-Time Locations Health Science Campus College Toledo, OH, Ohio, United Sta